<title>USA: Wesley Jessen to market lenses in Japan.</title>
<headline>Wesley Jessen to market lenses in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>DES PLAINES, Ill. 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wesley Jessen VisionCare Inc said Tuesday it has been granted approval by Japan's Ministry of Health and Welfare to begin marketing Precision UV disposable lenses in Japan.</p>
<p>The lenses will be marketed by Wesley Jessen's Japanese subsidiary, the company said.</p>
<p>The approval marks Wesley Jesson's entry into the disposable lens market in Japan, which is estimated to generate more than $100 million in sales annually, it said.</p>
<p>The company has been marketing its line of conventional contact lenses in Japan through the 1990s, it said.</p>
<p>	 ((-- Reuter Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
